// Calling a variable. This is the last thing the registry can answer: a
// called name that is no function of this program and no builtin, but *is*
// somebody's variable, is a variable used as if it were a function -- which is
// the one case idc.py singles out from "no such function" -- unless its type is
// a function type, when calling it is what it is for (value.id).

acc_callee(int id, string owner, int ln) {
  if(k_of(id) == "call" && is_call_var(id)) {
    acc_call_var(id, owner, ln);
  }
  acc_callee2(id, owner, ln);
} return void;

// Not a function of this program and not a builtin. The builtins whose return
// type ../../../../../../types/type_of/ already knows are asked there rather than
// listed again; the rest are the ones whose type it has never needed -- the
// list mutators, and the terminal and clock calls, which are used for their
// effect. Should that list ever fall behind idc.py's, it falls behind in the
// safe direction: an unlisted builtin makes this check quieter, never louder.
is_unknown_fn(string name) {
  int ok = 0;
  if(find_str((import fnames), name) < 0 && builtin_type(name) == "?" && name != "push" && name != "pop" && name != "put" && name != "flush" && name != "getkey" && name != "sleep_ms" && name != "ticks") {
    ok = 1;
  }
} return int ok;
given env_init ("nope"):(1)
given env_init ("push"):(0)

report_call_var(string name, string owner, int ln) {
  string loc_at_v = loc_at(owner, ln);
  print(loc_at_v + "'" + name + "' is a variable, not a function");
  note_failure();
} return void;
given regrow_d ("z", "f", 10):() then check_failed:(1)
given regrow_d ("y", "g", 20):() then check_failed:(1)
